<title>HONG KONG: Wheelock interim net down 47.88 pct.</title>
<headline>Wheelock interim net down 47.88 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   39.1	 vs 75.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    11.5	 vs 11.5</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  118.9 gain vs 24.8 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    788.0	vs 1,511.8</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,571.8    vs 1,122.7</p>
<p>    Company name		 Wheelock &amp; Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  January 24-29, 1997</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   January 31, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Wheelock is an investment holding company which engages in property investment, retailing, hotel operations and manufacturing.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$152.6 million on disposal of assets by an associated company and a gain of HK$36.3 million on disposal of long-term investments and loss of HK$70 million on costs relating to closing down of store operations.</p>
<p>Results of New Asia Realty and Trust Co Ltd, previously an associated company, have been consolidated into the group upon becoming a subsidiary on August 14, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
